<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Bitlis</h1><p class="st-meta">1182 CE – 1849 CE (approx.) · capital Bitlis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kurdish emirate that ruled Bitlis for centuries and produced Sharaf Khan Bidlisi, author of the Sharafnama, the first history of the Kurds.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitlis">Bitlis</a>, at a gorge south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a>, came under the Rojiki, a Kurdish tribal confederation, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> claimed descent from ancient Kurdish lords. Their rule is traditionally dated from the late 12th century, though early details rest on the family's own later history.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitlis">Bitlis</a> castle over a mountain district controlling the road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>. After 1514 they accepted Ottoman suzerainty with hereditary autonomy, alternating between Ottoman and Safavid sides. Emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharaf-khan-bidlisi">Sharaf Khan Bidlisi</a> completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharafnama">Sharafnama</a> in Persian in 1597, a history of Kurdish dynasties. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evliya-celebi">Evliya Celebi</a> described the rich court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdal-khan">Abdal Khan</a> in 1655, shortly before an Ottoman army attacked him.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 19th-century Ottoman centralisation the hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> were removed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bitlis">Bitlis</a> was placed under appointed governors by 1849.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-bitlis.jpg" alt="Emirate of Bitlis" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Taysheyi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roj_emblem.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1182 CE – 1849 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bitlis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sharaf Khan Bidlisi, Abdal Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kurdish, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rojiki emirate, Bitlis Kurdish emirate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1516&amp;focus=emirate-of-bitlis" aria-label="Emirate of Bitlis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5727 799 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Bitlis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6047 1055L6003 1071M6047 1055L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6003 1071h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6047 1055h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6047 1055h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bitlis. <a href="/atlas?year=1516&amp;focus=emirate-of-bitlis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

